ions for loading and subsequent DNA duplex unwinding [[cite:PUB00076694]]. It forms a complex with NurA nuclease, this complex has the 5'-3' DNA end resection activity and is essential for cell viability in the crenarchaeon Sulfolobus islandicus [[cite:PUB00076695]]. This domain includes the the central RecA-like catalytic core and a flanking four-helix bundle [[cite:PUB00078094]]. The function of this prokaryotic domain is unknown. It contains several conserved aspartates and histidines that could be metal ligands.","domain_architectures":87,"interpro_id":"IPR002789","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":11481,"name":"Helicase HerA, central domain","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF01935","proteins":11479,"proteomes":6966,"short_name":"DUF87","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF01935","structures":38,"taxa":11524,"unknown_status":"KNOWN_HISTORICAL_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"SEEDED","local_source":"source/data/families/PF01935.yaml","record":{"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":7658,"domain_architectures":87,"matches":11481,"proteins":11479,"proteomes":6966,"structures":38,"taxa":11524},"curation_status":"SEEDED","description":"This entry represents the central domain found in archaeal proteins such as DNA double-strand break repair helicase HerA ([ec:3.6.4.12]). HerA is a helicase which is able to utilise either 3' or 5' single-stranded DNA extensions for loading and subsequent DNA duplex unwinding [[cite:PUB00076694]]. It forms a complex with NurA nuclease, this complex has the 5'-3' DNA end resection activity and is essential for cell viability in the crenarchaeon Sulfolobus islandicus [[cite:PUB00076695]]. This domain includes the the central RecA-like catalytic core and a fla